<title>USA: Harris rescinds buyback plan after ruling.</title>
<headline>Harris rescinds buyback plan after ruling.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE, Fla. 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Harris Corp said on Friday it rescinded its share-buyback program due to a U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission ruling about when companies can use the pooling-of-interest accounting method when making acquisitions.</p>
<p>Harris has already repurchased about 500,000 of the 1.5 million shares it authorized for repurchase in 1995.</p>
<p>Harris is a communications and electronics firm.</p>
</text>
